    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd2 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd2 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bae\u0bb0\u0b9a\u0bc2\u0bb0\u0bbf\u0baf) \u0bbf\u0baf) (The Hon. (Dr.) Harini Amarasuriya) Hon. Speaker, as was mentioned, this is a very old project started in 2016 and came to a halt in 2020. As a result, there are several problems arisen with the contractors. The contracts they entered into are problematic and do not reflect current prices. So, there is a lot of negotiations to be done in order to restart the project. In 2025 and 2026, actually what our Government did was to review all of these projects, look at the contracts and wherever possible, negotiate with the existing contractors to come to some kind of agreement to complete these projects. So, both in 2025 and 2026, the Budget allocation was for their completion. The main portion for education infrastructure from the Budget was allocated to actually complete these incomplete projects. When we were doing that, we had to make a decision about some of the buildings which are now unusable and have to be abandoned. For those that could be continued with, we have allocated money, but the process is not as fast as we would like it to be simply because of the contractual problems. These are really old projects which had been abandoned and we have to renegotiate and restart them. Wherever possible, we have asked the principals not to use the buildings, if those are unsafe, till some decision could be made. But, if the Hon. Member has information about a specific school building which is incomplete and is unsafe, please let me know, and we will look into it.\n\n\u0b8e\u0ba9\u0ba4\u0bc1 \u0b87\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bbe\u0bb5\u0ba4\u0bc1 \u0bae\u0bc7\u0bb2\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b95 \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bbe\u0bb5\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bc7\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc7\u0ba9\u0bcd. \u0ba9\u0bcd."
  },
